<title>BELGIUM: RENAULT, BELGIAN UNIONS AGREE SOCIAL PLAN.</title>
<headline>RENAULT, BELGIAN UNIONS AGREE SOCIAL PLAN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French car maker Renault and unions at its plant in Vilvoorde, Belgium have reached agreement on a social plan for the closure of the plan, Belgian radio said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The radio said the plan offered workers a combination of unemployment payments, cash premiums and jobs for 400 workers on the Vilvoorde site.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be 400 jobs, but we regret they will not be industrial jobs,&quot; union leader Karel Gacoms told Belgian radio.</p>
<p>The radio said the 400 jobs would be mainly in maintenance and other support functions.</p>
</text>
